  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF TWO PROPERTIES FOR NMB ON THE APPALACHIAN CORRIDOR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will aid in the conservation of neotropical migratory birds through the acquisition of two tracts in Quebecs Appalachian Corridor. In the long term, the project aims to protect 10% of the Appalachian Corridors target area, based on landscape-scale conservation analyses and priorities, and maintain or increase local and regional populations of neotropical migratory birds species such as wood thrush, black-throated blue warbler, American woodcock, ruffed grouse, and rose-breasted grosbeak.</narrative>
  </description>
